From: WPE4YDPv2 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: fully skip player audio for delayed-track diagnosis

The existing WEBKIT_GST_WEBRTC_DISABLE_PLAYER_AUDIO switch clears playbin's
audio flag but still exposes an audio appsrc. If the remote audio track has no
sample yet, uridecodebin3 cannot discover its caps and the combined
MediaStream player remains pending PAUSED, so its ready video track never
reaches the final sink.

When the diagnostic switch is enabled, do not add audio tracks to the
MediaStream playback source. The WebRTC receiver and DataChannel remain
untouched. This makes the switch an actual video-only diagnostic and is
reversible independently of normal playback.

---
 .../gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaStreamSource.cpp
@@ -82,6 +82,12 @@ static bool reparseIncomingH264()
     return value && !g_strcmp0(value, "1");
 }
 
+static bool disableMediaStreamPlayerAudio()
+{
+    const char* value = g_getenv("WEBKIT_GST_WEBRTC_DISABLE_PLAYER_AUDIO");
+    return value && !g_strcmp0(value, "1");
+}
+
 [[nodiscard]] GRefPtr<GstTagList> mediaStreamTrackPrivateGetTags(const RefPtr<MediaStreamTrackPrivate>& track)
 {
     auto tagList = adoptGRef(gst_tag_list_new_empty());
@@ -1551,6 +1557,10 @@ void webkitMediaStreamSrcSetStream(WebKitMediaStreamSrc* self, MediaStreamPrivat
     for (auto& track : tracks) {
         if (!isVideoPlayer && track->isVideo())
             continue;
+        if (isVideoPlayer && track->isAudio() && disableMediaStreamPlayerAudio()) {
+            GST_WARNING_OBJECT(self, "Skipping MediaStream player audio source for delayed-track diagnosis");
+            continue;
+        }
         webkitMediaStreamSrcAddTrack(self, track.ptr(), isVideoPlayer);
     }
 
